# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/exact-end window (exact resume P0 on the production stack; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/exact-end and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-xe-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-xe-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory, in the prefix gate's
# containers too (c2_prefix_gate.py reads every arm's log for the checkpoint lines and fails the arm without them); the keys are the same in every serving job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone.
# SP1 (SOFT; the decision gate for everything that resumes OFF the 2048 grid, docs/tp4-exact-end.md 2 and 5): tp4_split_probe.py --attribute under the ship-4 candidate's
# own environment, from the checkout, inside the window image (the probe needs no build: it uses only the image's model code, the C2 graft and the G1 stage; it may also run
# before B0 on any existing four-card image). The model is the first real layers of the checkpoint up to and including the first full-attention layer; per synthetic prompt
# length (9,000 and 41,000) the arms A (cold), A2 (determinism control), C (split at a 2048 multiple, the harness control), B+128, B+1024, B+1920 and Bend (splits at
# 128-aligned R inside a chunk, each segment in the bucket the engine would pick) and F+128, F+1024, F+1920 and Fend (the same splits with BOTH segments forced into the
# 2048 bucket, the cold run's own program masked to the valid rows). READ the lines "SPLIT_PROBE attribution L= R= B+x=... F+x=... cause=...": cause=bucket (B differs, F
# identical) means the segments' PROGRAMS differ (another bucket is another matmul program config: a resume at R is exact only in the cold run's own bucket, which saves
# nothing over P0); cause=handoff (F differs) means the STORE at R (the bf16 GDN state and the conv carry) or the mask is not the cold run's own, whatever the bucket (a
# kernel that emits the in-program state is the only exact way); cause=none on every split means a 128-aligned resume IS byte-exact and the verdict line says IDENTICAL
# (then Option A of the doc needs no owner decision on exactness). DIFFERS is a valid measured answer (exit 2, the step ends red); FAIL (exit 1) is no answer (a control
# differed, the mesh did not open, an error: read split-probe.json). A failed run needs a reset before the next hardware job. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED (the weight load is the
# long part). Duration (estimate): 30 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset fabric
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-xe-1
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=split-attribute
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
